<DocsLayout title="Honeypot Engine" description="The WordPress layer, pool scaling, per-IP stickiness, seeding, backups" section="Engine" sidebar={sidebar} toc={toc}>
  <h2 id="overview">Engine Overview</h2>
  <p>The honeypot engine is the WordPress/WooCommerce layer that provides the high-interaction deception environment. It includes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>WordPress / WooCommerce Layer</strong> — Production and honeypot pool instances running full WordPress with WooCommerce, Elementor, and a real product catalog.</li>
    <li><strong>Pool Scaling & Assignment</strong> — Elastic honeypot pools cloned from a pre-built template, assigned per user session.</li>
    <li><strong>Seeding the Storefront</strong> — Product catalog, users, and content seeded for realism.</li>
    <li><strong>Backups</strong> — Backup and restore procedures for honeypot instances.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Content derived from the old mkdocs documentation in <code>docs-mkdocs-old/docs/engine/</code>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
